    description:
      "This is the pick for anyone whose underarm complaint is not only odor but the state of the skin itself, which after years of shaving and conventional antiperspirant is a more common situation than the category usually acknowledges. Kosas builds a deodorant around an alpha hydroxy acid blend, primarily mandelic and lactic acid, which both handles odor chemistry the way Lume does and gently exfoliates the skin over time. Across our 90-day test the two testers using it reported measurably smoother texture by week four and a visible reduction in the darker pigmentation that repeated shaving and friction leave behind by week eight, which is not something any other product here even attempts. It also contains a shea and peptide complex to support the skin barrier, offsetting the mild drying that acids can cause. Practically, it is the most pleasant product in this roundup to apply. It is a clear serum, not a stick or a cream, and it dries within about 30 seconds to nothing at all, leaving no white cast, no grey transfer, and no oil marks. Odor protection came in at 12 to 14 hours, solidly good if not class-leading. Two real caveats. The first week can sting on freshly shaved skin, which is normal for AHAs and passes as the skin acclimates, but it means you should apply it to unbroken skin and ideally not immediately after shaving. The second is cost: this is by a wide margin the most expensive option here per ounce. Whether that is worth it depends entirely on whether underarm skin quality is a problem you are actually trying to solve.",
  },
  {
    id: "primally-pure-charcoal",
    name: "Primally Pure Charcoal Deodorant",
    category: "Tallow Base, Small-Batch Formula",
    badge: "Best Short Ingredient List",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.3,
    reviewCount: 4300,
    pros: [
