    ],
    bottomLine:
      "For the buyer whose priority is the shortest, cleanest ingredient list available. Skip it if baking soda has ever caused you trouble.",
    description:
      "Primally Pure is the pick for the reader who came to natural deodorant primarily out of ingredient concerns rather than skin ones, and who wants a label they can read in full in about four seconds. The formula is five ingredients: grass-fed tallow, non-GMO arrowroot, baking soda, activated charcoal, and essential oils. There are no emulsifiers, no synthetic preservatives, no fillers to bulk out the stick, and nothing on the label that requires a search to identify. The tallow base is the unusual choice and it turns out to be a functional one rather than a marketing one. Tallow's fatty acid profile is closer to human sebum than plant oils are, and in practice it absorbs faster and leaves less of a film than the coconut oil bases that dominate this category, which meant less transfer onto shirts across our test. Odor control is genuinely strong, in the 13 to 15 hour range, with the baking soda and charcoal working on the problem from two directions at once. That baking soda is also the limitation, and it is a real one at this price: if you are among the sizable group whose skin reacts to alkaline formulas, this will not work for you, and Primally Pure's baking-soda-free version trades away a noticeable amount of the duration. The other honest caveat is availability and cost. It is a small-batch product sold mainly direct, it costs roughly three times a drugstore natural stick, and the glass-and-metal packaging that makes it appealing also makes it heavier and more fragile in a gym bag. Buy it for the ingredient list, with clear eyes about the trade-offs attached.",
  },
  {
    id: "dove-zero-aluminum",
